decisions:
  - id: ftux-tier-1
    decision: Nora (ftux) is tier-1 (opus)
    rationale: Simulating human cognition for first-time user walkthrough requires best-in-class reasoning
  - id: verdicts-durable
    decision: Verdicts stored in durable verdicts.jsonl separate from session-log.jsonl
    rationale: session-log.jsonl is cleared on session start, causing verdicts to be lost before postflight runs
  - id: notebook-ids-deterministic
    decision: Notebook IDs use nb-{agentId}-{conceptSlug} format — no timestamps
    rationale: nevr.land merge-by-id algorithm requires stable IDs across republishes
  - id: schema-ownership
    decision: '@a-company/agent-format owns NotebookEntry canonical schema'
    rationale: Prevents type drift between Paradigm and nevr.land publish pipeline
